 "research": "Proven 30 deg incline body (incline_dumbbell_press). Start: arms open level with the shoulders (elev 85, plane -10, elbow 20 fixed), handles in line with the chest; end: arms brought up and together over the upper chest (elev 95, plane 90, elbow 20 curving in, hands ~0.2 m apart). Vertical neutral handles along the torso (pec deck style), so the palms face forward then each other. Levers from the handle tops to a pivot above each shoulder (equal length start/end). Solstad 2020 (fly vs press EMG), Rodriguez-Ridao 2020 (30 deg incline favours the clavicular pec).",
